    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "Following her creative residency at Transcultures (Centre of digital and sound arts, Saint-Ghislain, Belgium) in October 2024, sound artist Joyul (Seoul-South Korea) presented an improvised performance centered around the daxophone (an instrument invented by German musician Hans Reichel\u2014a wooden tongue mounted on a tripod with contact microphones, played with a bow and a dax, a curved piece of wood, one side of which is fretted) in the vibrant environment of the baroque Chapel of the Convent of Hautrage.\nWith the support of Transcultures &amp; European Pepinieres of Cr\u00e9ation",
